    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nLocated on the highly regarded Albert Road in the heart of Sandycove, 68A Albert Road is a most attractive Victorian villa-style residence occupying a wonderfully private setting amidst beautifully mature gardens. Brimming with character and original charm, this unique home presents a rare opportunity to acquire a property of exceptional potential in one of South County Dublin's most sought-after residential addresses.\n\nSet behind a delightful front garden, the property immediately captivates with its timeless appeal. Beyond the attractive façade lies a bright and welcoming interior extending to generously proportioned accommodation, offering the perfect canvas for those wishing to create a truly exceptional family home.\n\nUpon entering, one is greeted by a spacious entrance hallway which sets the tone for the accommodation throughout. To the front of the property are four beautifully proportioned rooms, all flooded with natural light and currently arranged as bedrooms. The accommodation further comprises a spacious living room, kitchen/dining room and bathroom. A useful home office completes the accommodation. The flexible layout allows purchasers to reimagine the internal arrangement to suit modern family living requirements.\n\nWhile the property would benefit from modernisation and upgrading, it offers enormous scope to create a stunning family residence of distinction. Of particular note are the exceptional front and rear gardens. The large private rear garden is a wonderful feature and is further enhanced by a detached block-built garage and valuable rear access. The extensive site offers exciting potential for extension and further development, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nThe location is simply second to none. Situated within easy walking distance of the charming villages of Sandycove and Glasthule, residents can enjoy an enviable selection of cafés, restaurants, boutique shops and coastal amenities. The DART is quite literally on your doorstep, providing swift access to Dublin City Centre and beyond, while the stunning seafront and its wealth of recreational facilities are only a short stroll away.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a property of immense character and potential in a location that consistently ranks amongst the most desirable in Dublin. For those seeking to invest in a forever family home and create something truly special, 68A Albert Road represents an exceptional opportunity."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Special Features</li><li> Charming Victorian villa-style family home</li><li> Four generously proportioned bedrooms</li><li> One bathroom</li><li> Exceptional potential for modernisation and upgrading</li><li> Huge scope for extension and further development (subject to planning permission)</li><li> Large private rear garden</li><li> Beautiful mature front garden</li><li> Valuable rear access</li><li> Detached block-built garage</li><li> Bright and flexible accommodation throughout</li><li> Spacious entrance hallway</li><li> Gas-fired central heating</li><li> Excellent family home opportunity</li><li> On-street parking</li><li> Walking distance to Sandycove and Glasthule Villages</li><li> DART station within minutes' walk</li><li> Close to the seafront and numerous recreational amenities</li><li> Highly sought-after residential location in South County Dublin</li><li> Rare opportunity to create a bespoke family residence on a substantial site</ul>"
      },
